Troubleshoot and fix a hostname resolution failure where `curl http://localhost:3000` fails.

Requirements:
- Located in `/app`, you will find `app.py` and `Dockerfile`.
- Executing `curl http://127.0.0.1:3000` succeeds, but `curl http://localhost:3000` fails with `curl: (7) Failed to connect to localhost port 3000: Connection refused`.
- Diagnose why requests to `localhost` are failing (check hostname resolution in `/etc/hosts` or `ping localhost`).
- Fix `/etc/hosts` so that `localhost` correctly resolves to `127.0.0.1`.
- Verify that `curl http://localhost:3000` returns `OK - WebApp Healthy` with HTTP status code 200.
